{"cards.27.card.light_astro.headline.direct_to_dog": "Your Mars Wants a Brave, Sparkly Mission", "cards.27.card.light_astro.headline.handler": "Mars in Leo Turns Adventure Into a Performance", "cards.28.card.light_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Mars wants the chase, the display, and the immediate action. Pluto may notice a deeper detail and ask you to stop everything until it is understood. That strange switch is part of your pattern, not a reason to scold yourself. Let your person offer a small investigation and a clear release. You can be intense and playful, in that order.", "cards.28.card.light_astro.body.handler": "Pluto brings deep trust, fixation, and serious attention to local cues, while Mars in Leo brings visible chase and play. Their quincunx can produce an awkward gear change in which play suddenly feels consequential. Use decompression and structured searches, then a low-intensity restart. Ella does not need less enthusiasm; she needs help moving between seriousness and action.", "cards.28.card.light_astro.body.hybrid": "Ella's Pluto–Mars quincunx can make a playful moment unexpectedly weighty. Her person may try to restore fun by increasing energy, but a quieter recalibration often works better. Pause the chase, give the serious attention a safe task, and use a release cue before restarting. The relationship protects the game by respecting the interruption.", "cards.28.card.light_astro.headline.direct_to_dog": "Your Pluto Can Read the Fine Print Before Mars Plays Again", "cards.28.card.light_astro.headline.handler": "Pluto Makes Mars Stop for the Fine Print", "cards.28.card.light_astro.headline.hybrid": "A Pause Can Preserve the Game", "cards.29.card.light_astro.headline.direct_to_dog": "Your Favorite Person Is Part of the Game—and Part of the Rest", "cards.29.card.light_astro.headline.handler": "The Companion Bond Can Press the Mars Button", "cards.33.card.no_astro.headline.hybrid": "Ella Brings the Neighborhood News", "cards.34.card.no_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Ella, you already notice more than most rooms can hide. Training does not ask you to stop noticing. It gives your noticing a path: find the clue, look back, follow the cue, finish the task. Each repetition makes the path easier to travel, until your nose and your person are working on the same sentence.", "cards.34.card.no_astro.body.handler": "Ella’s attention to scent, sound, and small cues can look like competition for the handler’s focus. It may be more useful to treat it as the opening of a training channel. First let her notice. Then mark the moment she turns back, follows a simple cue, or uses the information in a structured search. Keep the sequence short and repeatable: notice, orient, act, release. Over time, her scanning becomes less of a detour and more of a conversation. The goal is not to make her less perceptive; it is to help perception lead somewhere.", "cards.34.card.no_astro.body.hybrid": "Ella catches a scent and starts to follow its story. Her person does not erase the story; they place a cue beside it. Ella notices, turns, performs the next step, and receives a reward. The exchange repeats until the scent is no longer a rival for attention. It has become the first word in a shared game.", "cards.34.card.no_astro.headline.direct_to_dog": "Your Nose Can Learn a Route", "cards.34.card.no_astro.headline.handler": "Train the Nose You Already Have", "cards.34.card.no_astro.headline.hybrid": "From Clue to Cue", "cards.35.card.no_astro.headline.hybrid": "The Three-Inch Solution", "cards.39.card.light_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Ella, your Mars wants motion, pursuit, and a little audience. Your visible pack role makes play a way of joining everyone. Your safe den gives the motion a beginning and an end. Run proudly, return willingly, and let the next game start from safety.", "cards.40.card.light_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Your Mercury notices the fine print: scent, tone, footsteps, sequence. With the North Node beside it, that noticing can become a social skill. You can inspect the world and still return to the group. Let one gentle cue be your bridge from private investigation to a choice made with us.", "cards.40.card.light_astro.body.handler": "Mercury in Virgo gives Ella an attentive, discriminating way of reading cues, while the North Node in Libra points that attention toward social cooperation. She may investigate first and then look for the response that keeps the group in balance. Make that pathway usable: offer one clear cue, let her process, and reinforce the calm return to the shared activity.", "cards.40.card.light_astro.body.hybrid": "Mercury in Virgo helps Ella sort the details; the North Node in Libra joins that sorting to relationship. In practice, a pause over local data can become a check-in rather than a detour. Her person makes room for the investigation, then gives her a fair, repeatable way to re-enter the shared task.", "cards.40.card.light_astro.headline.direct_to_dog": "Mercury Gives You a Way Back to Us", "cards.40.card.light_astro.headline.handler": "Mercury and the Learning Check-In", "cards.40.card.light_astro.headline.hybrid": "When Information Becomes Teamwork", "cards.41.card.light_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Your Jupiter in Virgo wants to explore, but it likes useful details along the way. You can widen the map one inspected corner at a time. Let your confidence be practical: discover, remember, and return ready to show your people what you found.", "cards.6.card.no_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Ella, the unexpected may arrive fast, but you do not have to solve it alone. A known cue, an interesting scent to read, and your person’s steady presence can turn the moment into something you understand.", "cards.6.card.no_astro.headline.hybrid": "Notice, Signal, Rejoin", "cards.7.card.no_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Ella, you pick up the fine print of a room. When your person gives that noticing a clear next move, you can show just how beautifully your attention works.", "cards.7.card.no_astro.body.handler": "Ella may catch details before you have decided they matter: a changed scent, a familiar pre-walk sound, a shift in your routine. Pair such alertness with one simple, practiced next step. Consistent cues let her turn observation into cooperation instead of carrying every detail by herself.", "cards.7.card.no_astro.body.hybrid": "Ella notices the small change first. You offer the familiar instruction. She follows the sequence, and a loose scrap of information becomes something the two of you can do together.", "cards.7.card.no_astro.headline.direct_to_dog": "Your Nose Loves a Good Rule", "cards.7.card.no_astro.headline.handler": "Give Her Noticing a Next Step", "cards.7.card.no_astro.headline.hybrid": "From Clue to Cue", "cards.8.card.no_astro.body.direct_to_dog": "Ella, you do not have to become everyone’s entertainment. You can learn when to approach, when to pause, and when a calm presence is your best contribution to the group.", "cards.8.card.no_astro.headline.hybrid": "A Little More Room for Everyone"}
